      "text": " ```json\n{\n    \"patterns\": [\n        {\n            \"pattern\": \"^[a-f][a-f]{2,4}$\",\n            \"flags\": \"\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\nThis pattern ensures only lowercase hexadecimal strings of length between three and five will match. It uses `^` at the start and `$` at the end as anchors to ensure we capture whole words from beginning to end without partial matches within larger texts. The `[a-f]` part specifies each digit must be an uppercase Latin alphabet letter ranging from 'A' through 'F'. `{2,4}` after it indicates there should be two more digits following this first one, making sure our string is either exactly four characters long (`[a-f]`) if starting with a capitalized letter like 'A', or up to six characters total when including additional lower case letters ('aa'). This setup covers both minimum lengths due to inclusive range specified by curly braces. Remember, since you requested exclusively lowercase letters but used mixed casing examples above, make sure your input strictly adheres to these constraints—or adjust accordingly based on actual requirements!",
